{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-21591","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21170","text":"The [&] Protocol Ecosystem"}]},{"id":"blk-21592","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21171","text":"This repository holds the [&] Protocol specification and every in-tree reference implementation of it, plus the portfolio products that build on top. This document is the one-page tour for someone trying to understand how the pieces fit."}]},{"id":"blk-21593","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21172","text":"For authoritative status — what's shipped, what's in progress, what the test counts are — see "},{"id":"spn-21173","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/STACK_COMPLETION.md"}],"text":"`STACK_COMPLETION.md`"},{"id":"spn-21174","text":"."}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-21595","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21175","marks":["bold"],"text":"Last substantive update 2026-06-10; three rulings have landed since."},{"id":"spn-21176","text":" (1) The shared-Supabase data layer was "},{"id":"spn-21177","marks":["bold"],"text":"abandoned 2026-07-30"},{"id":"spn-21178","text":" in favour of "},{"id":"spn-21179","marks":["code"],"text":"studbook"},{"id":"spn-21180","text":". (2) "},{"id":"spn-21181","marks":["bold"],"text":"Compute moves into the ComputeDriven OS"},{"id":"spn-21182","text":" (2026-08-15) — the Fly.io apps become storage or nothing. (3) "},{"id":"spn-21183","marks":["bold"],"text":"T&R is an operating system and the backup is the user's machine, 10 GB–10 TB."},{"id":"spn-21184","text":" The tour below still describes the pre-ruling shape. See "},{"id":"spn-21185","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"./REVISION_REGISTER.md"}],"text":"`REVISION_REGISTER.md`"},{"id":"spn-21186","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-21594","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-21596","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21187","text":"The stack, in one diagram"}]},{"id":"blk-21597","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"                      ┌──────────────────────────────────────┐\n                      │   [&] Protocol — composition algebra  │\n                      │    6 primitives · 2 operators        │\n                      │    (AmpersandBoxDesign/)             │\n                      └───────────────┬──────────────────────┘\n                                      │ compiles into\n                  ┌───────────────────┴────────────────────┐\n                  │                                        │\n          ┌───────┴────────┐                      ┌────────┴────────┐\n          │   MCP runtime  │                      │  A2A coordination│\n          │   transport    │                      │    transport      │\n          └───────┬────────┘                      └─────────────────┘\n                  │\n   ┌──────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────┐\n   │              │                                           │\n   │   OS protocols (OpenSentience) — 11 normative protocols  │\n   │   OS-001 Continual Learning  → Graphonomous              │\n   │   OS-002 κ-Routing           → Graphonomous              │\n   │   OS-003 Deliberation        → Graphonomous              │\n   │   OS-004 Attention           → Graphonomous              │\n   │   OS-005 Model Tier          → (system-level)            │\n   │   OS-006 Governance Shim     → delegatic                 │\n   │   OS-007 Adversarial         → (draft)                   │\n   │   OS-008 Agent Harness       → open_sentience            │\n   │   OS-009 PRISM benchmark     → PRISM                     │\n   │   OS-010 PULSE temporal      → PULSE                     │\n   │   GRASP                      → body-browser + body-os    │\n   └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"},{"id":"blk-21598","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21188","text":"The dark-factory closed loop"}]},{"id":"blk-21599","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21189","text":"The north-star use case for this stack is the "},{"id":"spn-21190","marks":["bold"],"text":"dark factory"},{"id":"spn-21191","text":": agents hosted on machines that operate autonomously, learn continually, and transfer skills to each other. Seven steps close the loop:"}]},{"id":"blk-21600","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │  1. Machine A perceives & acts           ←  body-browser     │\n  │                                              body-os         │\n  │  2. Records InteractionTrace             ←  Graphonomous     │\n  │     (&memory.episodic.store)                                 │\n  │                                                              │\n  │  3. Learns via memory consolidation       ←  Graphonomous    │\n  │     (consolidation, κ-routing)                               │\n  │                                                              │\n  │  4. Crystallizes to SkillCandidate        ←  FleetPrompt     │\n  │     (Crystallizer + Oban PollWorker +                        │\n  │      GraphonomousClient.HTTP)                                │\n  │                                                              │\n  │  5. Ships via FleetPrompt                 ←  FleetPrompt     │\n  │     (Registry, Trust, InstallEngine)                         │\n  │                                                              │\n  │  6. Machine B installs + replays          ←  body-browser    │\n  │     (with fresh authorization on             body-os         │\n  │      destructive edges per GRASP §4.4)       delegatic       │\n  │                                              (authorizer)    │\n  │                                                              │\n  │  7. PRISM measures                        ←  PRISM           │\n  │     (GRASP scenario suite,                                   │\n  │      BYOR cross-system benchmark)                            │\n  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"},{"id":"blk-21601","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21192","text":"Current status (see "},{"id":"spn-21193","marks":["code"],"text":"STACK_COMPLETION.md"},{"id":"spn-21194","text":" for always-live detail): "},{"id":"spn-21195","marks":["bold"],"text":"7 of 7 steps fully in-tree"},{"id":"spn-21196","text":". Every step has implemented code paths, passing tests, and (for the MCP-exposed pieces) deployment configs."}]},{"id":"blk-21602","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21197","text":"Product map"}]},{"id":"blk-21603","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21198","text":"Shipping products"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-21605","spans":[{"id":"spn-21199","text":"Product"}]},{"id":"blk-21606","spans":[{"id":"spn-21200","text":"Role in the loop"}]},{"id":"blk-21607","spans":[{"id":"spn-21201","text":"Transport"}]},{"id":"blk-21608","spans":[{"id":"spn-21202","text":"Test count"}]}],"id":"blk-21604","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-21609","spans":[{"id":"spn-21203","text":"Graphonomous"}]},{"id":"blk-21610","spans":[{"id":"spn-21204","text":"episodic memory + continual learning engine"}]},{"id":"blk-21611","spans":[{"id":"spn-21205","text":"MCP (stdio/HTTP)"}]},{"id":"blk-21612","spans":[{"id":"spn-21206","text":"573"}]}],[{"id":"blk-21613","spans":[{"id":"spn-21207","text":"PULSE"}]},{"id":"blk-21614","spans":[{"id":"spn-21208","text":"temporal loop manifest standard"}]},{"id":"blk-21615","spans":[{"id":"spn-21209","text":"npm package"}]},{"id":"blk-21616","spans":[{"id":"spn-21210","text":"3"}]}],[{"id":"blk-21617","spans":[{"id":"spn-21211","text":"PRISM"}]},{"id":"blk-21618","spans":[{"id":"spn-21212","text":"cross-system CL benchmark"}]},{"id":"blk-21619","spans":[{"id":"spn-21213","text":"MCP + LiveView"}]},{"id":"blk-21620","spans":[{"id":"spn-21214","text":"172"}]}],[{"id":"blk-21621","spans":[{"id":"spn-21215","text":"[&] reference"}]},{"id":"blk-21622","spans":[{"id":"spn-21216","text":"protocol spec + Elixir CLI"}]},{"id":"blk-21623","spans":[{"id":"spn-21217","text":"CLI"}]},{"id":"blk-21624","spans":[{"id":"spn-21218","text":"58"}]}],[{"id":"blk-21625","spans":[{"id":"spn-21219","text":"body-browser"}]},{"id":"blk-21626","spans":[{"id":"spn-21220","marks":["code"],"text":"&body.browser"},{"id":"spn-21221","text":" provider (GRASP)"}]},{"id":"blk-21627","spans":[{"id":"spn-21222","text":"MCP (stdio/HTTP)"}]},{"id":"blk-21628","spans":[{"id":"spn-21223","text":"41"}]}],[{"id":"blk-21629","spans":[{"id":"spn-21224","text":"body-os"}]},{"id":"blk-21630","spans":[{"id":"spn-21225","marks":["code"],"text":"&body.os"},{"id":"spn-21226","text":" provider (GRASP)"}]},{"id":"blk-21631","spans":[{"id":"spn-21227","text":"MCP (stdio/HTTP)"}]},{"id":"blk-21632","spans":[{"id":"spn-21228","text":"41"}]}],[{"id":"blk-21633","spans":[{"id":"spn-21229","marks":["bold"],"text":"delegatic"}]},{"id":"blk-21634","spans":[{"id":"spn-21230","marks":["bold"],"text":"OS-006 authorization kernel"}]},{"id":"blk-21635","spans":[{"id":"spn-21231","marks":["bold"],"text":"MCP (stdio/HTTP)"}]},{"id":"blk-21636","spans":[{"id":"spn-21232","marks":["bold"],"text":"42"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-21637","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21233","text":"Progressing products (4)"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-21639","spans":[{"id":"spn-21234","text":"Product"}]},{"id":"blk-21640","spans":[{"id":"spn-21235","text":"Role"}]},{"id":"blk-21641","spans":[{"id":"spn-21236","text":"Tests"}]}],"id":"blk-21638","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-21642","spans":[{"id":"spn-21237","text":"Agentelic"}]},{"id":"blk-21643","spans":[{"id":"spn-21238","text":"spec-driven agent builder"}]},{"id":"blk-21644","spans":[{"id":"spn-21239","text":"66"}]}],[{"id":"blk-21645","spans":[{"id":"spn-21240","text":"FleetPrompt"}]},{"id":"blk-21646","spans":[{"id":"spn-21241","text":"marketplace + trust + install + crystallizer"}]},{"id":"blk-21647","spans":[{"id":"spn-21242","text":"121 (108 + 13 install tests)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-21648","spans":[{"id":"spn-21243","text":"SpecPrompt"}]},{"id":"blk-21649","spans":[{"id":"spn-21244","text":"spec-driven dev toolchain"}]},{"id":"blk-21650","spans":[{"id":"spn-21245","text":"93"}]}],[{"id":"blk-21651","spans":[{"id":"spn-21246","text":"RuneFort"}]},{"id":"blk-21652","spans":[{"id":"spn-21247","text":"spatial cognition visualization (SvelteKit)"}]},{"id":"blk-21653","spans":[{"id":"spn-21248","text":"—"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-21654","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21249","text":"Frontend apps (2)"}]},{"id":"blk-21655","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21250","text":"WebHost.Systems (React dashboard, 143 tests) and BendScript (SvelteKit KAG editor, 26 tests)."}]},{"id":"blk-21656","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21251","text":"Spec-only (5)"}]},{"id":"blk-21657","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21252","text":"AgenTroMatic (1118-line spec), Delegatic (630), Deliberatic (418), GeoFleetic (987), TickTickClock (1013)."}]},{"id":"blk-21658","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21253","text":"The three protocols in depth"}]},{"id":"blk-21659","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21254","text":"All three fit together as a three-layer stack:"}]},{"id":"blk-21660","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-21662","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21255","marks":["bold"],"text":"[&]"},{"id":"spn-21256","text":" (composition) — agents declare what capabilities they have via "},{"id":"spn-21257","marks":["code"],"text":".ampersand.json"},{"id":"spn-21258","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-21661","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-21664","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21259","marks":["bold"],"text":"PULSE"},{"id":"spn-21260","text":" (temporal) — agents declare how their capabilities circulate via "},{"id":"spn-21261","marks":["code"],"text":".pulse.json"},{"id":"spn-21262","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-21663","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-21666","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21263","marks":["bold"],"text":"PRISM"},{"id":"spn-21264","text":" (diagnostic) — benchmarks measure the loops over time."}]}],"id":"blk-21665","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-21667","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21265","text":"Example: Graphonomous declares its continual-learning loop in "},{"id":"spn-21266","marks":["code"],"text":"PULSE/manifests/graphonomous.continual_learning.json"},{"id":"spn-21267","text":"; PRISM reads that manifest directly to discover phases, signatures, and substrates — no separate benchmark config needed."}]},{"id":"blk-21668","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-21268","text":"Shared infrastructure"}]},{"id":"blk-21669","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-21671","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21269","marks":["bold"],"text":"Supabase"},{"id":"spn-21270","text":": single shared instance, "},{"id":"spn-21271","marks":["code"],"text":"fleet.*"},{"id":"spn-21272","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-21273","marks":["code"],"text":"kag.*"},{"id":"spn-21274","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-21275","marks":["code"],"text":"webhost.*"},{"id":"spn-21276","text":"/…/"},{"id":"spn-21277","marks":["code"],"text":"spec.*"},{"id":"spn-21278","text":" per-product schemas. One "},{"id":"spn-21279","marks":["code"],"text":"supabase start"},{"id":"spn-21280","text":" runs every product's data layer. "},{"id":"spn-21281","marks":["bold"],"text":"40"},{"id":"spn-21282","text":" migrations live in "},{"id":"spn-21283","marks":["code"],"text":"ampersand-supabase/migrations/"},{"id":"spn-21284","text":" (counted 2026-08-16; this said 35)."}]}],"id":"blk-21670","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-21673","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-21285","marks":["bold"],"text":"amp-nav"},{"id":"spn-21286","text":": Web Component distributed to every portfolio marketing site via "},{"id":"spn-21287","marks":["code"],"text":"sync-nav.sh"},{"id":"spn-21288","text":". Current version: "},{"id":"spn-21289","marks":["code"],"text":"v0.3.3"},{"id":"spn-21290","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-21672","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":